Why each file is here — none is aspirational:
  MIMXRT1062.h            included by fsl_device_registers.h line 26 under any of
                          the CPU_MIMXRT1062* macros.  np_application defines
                          CPU_MIMXRT1062DVL6A; no other branch is taken.
  MIMXRT1062_features.h   included by fsl_device_registers.h line 28, in the same
                          branch.  Verified by deletion: removing it fails the
                          compile.
  fsl_device_registers.h  included by system_MIMXRT1062.c line 67.  It is the only
                          thing that turns a CPU macro into a device header, so
                          the pair above cannot be used without it.
  system_MIMXRT1062.h     included by MIMXRT1062.h line 281; also declares
                          SystemInit(), which startup_MIMXRT1062.S calls.
  system_MIMXRT1062.c     defines SystemInit() (watchdog disable, cache enable,
                          SystemCoreClock).  Reset_Handler branches to it before
                          .data is copied, so there is no NeurOne-authored
                          substitute that would not be an invented clock
                          sequence for silicon nobody has run yet.
  gcc/startup_MIMXRT1062.S  the vector table the bootloader jumps through:
                          word 0 is the initial SP and word 1 the reset handler
                          (firmware/bootloader/src/np_main.c load_and_jump()).
                          Assembled with -D__STARTUP_CLEAR_BSS and -D__START=main
                          — see firmware/application/CMakeLists.txt for why.
  COPYING-BSD-3           the licence the files above are distributed under.

CMSIS-Core(M) is NOT duplicated here.  MIMXRT1062.h line 280 includes core_cm7.h,
which is vendored once at firmware/vendor/cmsis_core/ alongside the Cortex-M0+
header SW-01 uses.  One copy of a shared component, two SW items — see that
directory's VERSION record, which was revised on 2026-09-01 to say so.

Intentionally NOT vendored — named explicitly so a later reader does not read the
omissions as oversight:
  drivers/**              fsl_clock.c, fsl_iomuxc, fsl_lpi2c, fsl_lpspi, fsl_pwm,
                          fsl_adc, fsl_usdhc and the rest of the peripheral driver
                          set.  SW-02 makes zero fsl_* calls: verified by
                          word-boundary grep over firmware/ excluding vendor/,
                          which returns nothing outside comments.  The SW-02
                          platform layer that WOULD call them does not exist —
                          it is 92 unresolved symbols standing in for it
                          (NP-SW-CI-001 §4.8).  Vendoring drivers now would be
                          vendoring for a caller that has not been written, and
                          the subset could only be guessed.  Whichever drivers
                          that layer needs get vendored when it is written, under
                          the same obligations.
  boards/**, components/**, middleware/**, utilities/**, CMSIS_driver/**
                          board bring-up, USB/lwIP/FatFs stacks, debug console.
                          None is referenced by this repository.
  devices/MIMXRT1062/gcc/MIMXRT1062xxxxx_flexspi_nor.ld and every other SDK
  linker script          NOT vendored, and this is a decision rather than an
                          omission.  Every SDK script for this part links the
                          image for execution in place from FlexSPI NOR flash at
                          0x60000000.  NeurOne has no FlexSPI application image:
                          the bootloader reads the application out of an eMMC
                          bank into the OCRAM staging area and jumps to it
                          (np_main.c load_and_jump()).  A vendored linker script
                          that puts .text at 0x60000000 is not a starting point
                          for that, it is a trap.  NeurOne authors its own —
                          firmware/application/linker/app_imxrt1062.ld, whose
                          agreement with the bootloader's reservation is
                          enforced by np_app_link_agreement_tests rather than
                          asserted in a comment.
  devices/MIMXRT1062/drivers, /template, /project_template, .yml/.xml metadata
                          SDK packaging and tooling.
